---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Security" description="Security practices for Tangle services and customer data.">
  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 pt-32 pb-24">
    <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold">How Tangle protects its services</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-(--text-secondary) leading-relaxed">This page describes the security practices currently used for Tangle-operated services. It is not a certification statement or a guarantee of uninterrupted security.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-5 text-(--text-secondary) leading-relaxed">
      Tangle completed a SOC 2 Type II examination with A-LIGN covering June 14 to September 14, 2026; the report is in issuance.
      Current control status, the subprocessor list, and security FAQs are published on the <a class="underline text-fg" href="https://app.vanta.com/tangle.tools/trust/kzhjp5g62vhwoalztadtz" rel="noopener">Tangle Trust Center</a>.
      A Data Processing Agreement is available from <a class="underline text-fg" href="mailto:security@tangle.tools">security@tangle.tools</a>.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-16 space-y-12 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-(--text-secondary)">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-fg mb-3">Access and identity</h2>
        <p>Production administration is restricted to authorized personnel. Administrative access uses multi-factor authentication where the provider supports it, and production Linux hosts do not accept SSH password authentication. Tangle periodically reviews administrative access to its cloud, source-control, and collaboration systems.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-fg mb-3">Infrastructure and data protection</h2>
        <p>Public services use TLS in transit. Managed stores and Restic backups are encrypted at rest. Two self-managed dedicated hosts lack full-disk encryption and remain an open risk; the staging pair was decommissioned in September 2026. Backups run on scheduled jobs with retention rules, and restoration tests verify that backed-up database data can be read in an isolated environment.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-fg mb-3">Application security</h2>
        <p>Tangle uses source-control review, automated dependency monitoring, and vulnerability remediation workflows for its maintained repositories. Authentication endpoints enforce rate limits, and administrative actions are recorded in application audit logs.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-fg mb-3">Monitoring and incident response</h2>
        <p>Tangle collects application, database, operating-system, and edge-provider audit data. Security-relevant alerts and incidents are investigated according to the company incident-response process. Public service checks are published on the <a class="underline text-fg" href="/status/">status page</a>.</p>
      </section>
      <section id="hipaa">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-fg mb-3">HIPAA</h2>
        <p>HIPAA-covered workloads require signed vendor Business Associate Agreements and verified deployment safeguards before onboarding. To plan one, email <a class="underline text-fg" href="mailto:security@tangle.tools">security@tangle.tools</a>.</p>
        <p class="mt-3">Protections in place:</p>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc pl-6 space-y-1.5">
          <li>Zero-data-retention inference routing through the Tangle Router, which routes enrolled requests only through providers with verified agreements to delete request data after processing.</li>
          <li>Per-user encrypted vaults for health records, with encryption keys derived per user and a fail-closed posture when the vault key is absent.</li>
          <li>Append-only audit trails recording every read, write, export, and erasure of vault records.</li>
          <li>A Business Associate Agreement enrollment flow for app and team owners, available from the dashboard when an approved agreement is configured for the deployment.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3">The protection model and enrollment steps are documented in the <a class="underline text-fg" href="https://docs.tangle.tools/gateway/hipaa">HIPAA guide</a> in the Tangle documentation.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-fg mb-3">Report a vulnerability</h2>
        <p>To report a suspected vulnerability, email <a class="underline text-fg" href="mailto:security@tangle.tools">security@tangle.tools</a>. Do not include credentials or sensitive customer data in the initial report. We will acknowledge the report and coordinate a safe remediation path.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-fg mb-3">Related documents</h2>
        <p>See the <a class="underline text-fg" href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a>, <a class="underline text-fg" href="/terms-of-service/">Terms of Service</a>, and <a class="underline text-fg" href="/sub-processors/">sub-processor list</a> for the public terms that govern use of Tangle services.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
